  "quote_spans": [
    {
      "chunk_id": 35,
      "char_start": 961,
      "char_end": 1149,
      "text": "Never fear but Elizabeth shall hear\nevery word of your precious story--ay, and the captain, and the\nlieutenant, and Madam Beck, too; and you'll be hunted from the Juno like\na dripping cur"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 36,
      "char_start": 460,
      "char_end": 844,
      "text": "But the receiver in\nthe like is no better than the stealer,\" she resumed, indignantly; \"and\nI'd have you know, it was just Beck's own daughter who came here and\noffered Elizabeth a respectable place in a respectable house, and it was\nto me she talked, my lad,\" pointing self-consciously with quivering\nforefinger at her own bosom; \"so Elizabeth has not begged herself in\nthere at all"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 39,
      "char_start": 267,
      "char_end": 602,
      "text": "From the very first, Elizabeth, who, in her utter ignorance how to\nbehave, committed one egregious blunder after another, had perceived\nwith her strong sense that it would require all the cleverness and\npatience she possessed to enable her to maintain the situation; and she\nbegan by following Madam Beck about untiringly like a lamb"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 40,
      "char_start": 724,
      "char_end": 1212,
      "text": "Madam Beck herself bound up her hand in the kitchen, where she stood\nwhite with pain; while Carl, who had been sitting on the sofa, and had\nseen how the whole thing happened, forgetting his self-command, had\njumped up in great excitement, and had shown such uncommon sympathy that\nhis sister Mina, afterwards, when they were alone in the room together,\nsaid, with a look that was more searching than the joking words seemed\nto require, \"It is not possible you are fond of the girl, Carl"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": 43,
      "char_start": 642,
      "char_end": 958,
      "text": "All that had formed the ideal of her young\nenthusiasm had suddenly in his person appeared upon the rock; but\nwhether it was his uniform, or the bravery of the fleet, or himself,\nthat was the object of her admiration, she had never asked herself,\nuntil hurt and rendered thoughtful by that warning of her grandfather"
    }
  ],
